<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Boshin War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1868">1868</a>–<a href="/years/1869">1869</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Boshin War was a Japanese civil war fought in 1868–1869 between forces loyal to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-shogunate">Tokugawa shogunate</a> and a coalition led by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satsuma-domain">Satsuma</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/choshu-domain">Choshu</a> domains acting in the name of the emperor. The imperial forces defeated the shogunal army and its French-trained troops. The war ended the Tokugawa <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">Shogunate</a> and consolidated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meiji-restoration">Meiji Restoration</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/boshin-war.jpg" alt="Boshin War" width="320" height="157" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Utagawa Yoshimori · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:UenoSenso.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
